%$$((A_1, p_1, B_1), ..., (A_n, p_n, B_n)) \in E^{\mathcal{E}^{\mrm{ex}}_M(k)}_n$$
%and so $f: \mathcal{E}^{\mrm{ex}}_M(k) \cong \mathcal{E}^{\mrm{ex}}_N(k)$, this concludes the proof of item (1).
The fact that also the predicates $\mrm{Dom}$ and $\mrm{Cod}$ from \ref{def_expanded_12}(\ref{dom})(\ref{cod}) are preserved is easy. Concerning the $P_n$'s, for $1 \leq n < \omega$, observe the following:
	\[ \begin{array}{rcl}	
(A, B_1, ..., B_n) \in P^{\mathcal{E}^{\mrm{ex}}_M(k)}_n
& \Leftrightarrow &  A \subseteq \mrm{acl}^{\mrm{g}}_M(B_1 \cup \cdots B_n) \\
& \Leftrightarrow &  G_{(\mrm{acl}^{\mrm{g}}_M(B_1 \cup \cdots B_n))} \leq G_{(A)} \\
& \Leftrightarrow     &  H_{(\mrm{acl}^{\mrm{g}}_N(f(B_1) \cup \cdots f(B_n)))} \leq H_{f(A)} \\
& \Leftrightarrow     &  f(A) \subseteq \mrm{acl}^{\mrm{g}}_N(f(B_1) \cup \cdots f(B_n)) \\
