\subsection*{IntFold+}

To create IntFold+, a model specialized for high-quality antibody-antigen and protein-ligand prediction, we performed a dedicated fine-tuning procedure on the base IntFold model. For this stage, we augmented the training data by including our curated antibody-antigen distillation set~\ref{section:data_source}. We also modified the training protocol by increasing the batch size, removing the MSA pairing information for antibody-antigen complexes to force a greater reliance on structural features, adjusting the ratio of nucleic data, and masking regions with low pLDDT. This combination of data enrichment and a specialized training strategy results in a model highly optimized for the nuances of antibody-antigen docking and protein-ligand binding. While we have demonstrated the effectiveness of these components, a detailed ablation study to quantify the individual contribution of each modification—such as the best data recipe, removal of MSA pairing, and pLDDT masking—remains an area for future work.



