Despite the fact that secondary particles will likely cause issues with deconvolution, it can be seen in \cref{fig:GLE_GCR_pulse_height} that the different radiation sources do generate quite different pulse height spectra (PHS) in the detectors. The difference between the GCR proton PHS, and the PHS for the two GLE spectra have very different shapes (for instance for a photon count of 79.8 the PHS of GLE05 is 209.6 times greater than that of GLE21, whereas at a photon count of 263.6, the PHS of GLE05 is 458.7 times larger), which indicates that spectral deconvolution of photon channels would likely be possible assuming background due to trapped particles and other sources is not significant.

