\section{Conclusion} \label{sec:conclusion}
In this paper, we have presented MULTI-SCOUT that repurposes standard 5G PRS waveforms for high-accuracy multistatic sensing and tracking of moving targets. By extracting coherent range and Doppler measurements
across distributed receivers,
MULTI-SCOUT delivers fine-grained 2D and 3D 
positioning, inter-receiver clock calibration, and target association across distributed receivers.
The position estimates are then processed by standard KF or EKF for target tracking under different motion models. Overall, MULTI-SCOUT provides high-fidelity moving target detection, positioning, and tracking using the existing 5G PRS signals without relying on additional sensing capabilities. 


