This order is then revised by a model $J$ of $G(1)$. If $J$ differs from $I$,
it is in the last class and the result is $\formulaorder{\{J\}} = [\{J\}, \true
\{J\}]$ by Lemma~\ref{lemma-plainsevere-last}. If it coincides with $I$, then
its only minimal model is $I$ itself: $\min(\{J\}) = \{J\}$ and $\imin(\{J\}) =
0$.

\begin{eqnarray*}
\lefteqn{\formulaorder{\{J\}} \psev(\{J\})}
\\
&=&
[
	\min(\{J\}),
	C(0) \cup \cdots \cup C(\imin(\{J\})+1) \backslash \min(\{J\}),
	C(\imin(\{J\})+2), \ldots, C(\last)
]
\\
&=&
[
	\{J\},
	C(0) \cup \cdots \cup C(0+1) \backslash \{J\},
	C(0+2), \ldots, C(1)
]
\\
&=&
[
	\{J\},
	C(0) \cup \cdots \cup C(1) \backslash \{J\}
]
\\
&=&
[
	\{J\},
	\true \backslash \{J\}
]
\\
&=&
	\formulaorder{\{J\}}
\end{eqnarray*}

