\subsection{Hotspots in planar geodesic orbits}

In order to examine the possibility that the non-Keplerian indication could deviate from the non-circular motion, we further fit the flare motions using non-circular geodesic orbits confined to the accretion disks. %The results are shown in Fig.~\ref{non-circular orbits} and Fig.~\ref{non-circular orbits-1}. 
Fig.~\ref{non-circular orbits} presents the posterior distributions for this model. There is no strong anti-correlation between the black hole mass and the orbital radius.
With the $\chi_\text{eff}^2=0.14$, the fit remains as good as  that of the circular orbit case. In Tab.~\ref{T3}, we present the posterior median values of the parameters and the corresponding uncertainty for the planar geodesic orbits.
